Subject: [PATCH] rocjitsu: reach dup2 through SYS_dup3 where SYS_dup2 is absent

aarch64 Linux carries no dup2 syscall -- glibc implements dup2() on top of
dup3() -- so SYS_dup2 is undefined there and the KMD interposer fails to
compile. dup3(oldfd, newfd, 0) is defined to behave as dup2 for distinct
descriptors, which is the only case this branch reaches.

--- a/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/kmd/linux/interposer.cpp
+++ b/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/kmd/linux/interposer.cpp
@@
-    return static_cast<int>(syscall(SYS_dup2, oldfd, newfd));
+#ifdef SYS_dup2
+    return static_cast<int>(syscall(SYS_dup2, oldfd, newfd));
+#else
+    // aarch64 and other newer ports expose only dup3; flags=0 matches dup2
+    // semantics, and oldfd == newfd is handled by the caller below.
+    return static_cast<int>(syscall(SYS_dup3, oldfd, newfd, 0));
+#endif
